# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
# The builder stage only needs go.mod, go.sum, and the Go source under
# api/, cmd/, internal/, pkg/ - the final image ships just the compiled
# binary, so nothing else here reaches it either way. Excluding the rest
# keeps the build context small and avoids invalidating the go-build layer
# cache on unrelated changes (docs, CI config, tooling, etc).
.git
.github
.devcontainer
.claude
.dockerignore
.gitignore
.golangci.yml
.custom-gcl.yml
bin
dist
config
containers
test
docs
hack
Dockerfile
LICENSE
Makefile
*.md
*.out
renovate.json
PROJECT

# Go test files don't affect the compiled binary
**/*_test.go
